Description: Dynamic Compact Control Language (development files)
 The Dynamic Compact Control Language (DCCL) is a marshalling and protocol
 language for very low throughput links (e.g. acoustic, satellite, low
 frequency radio).
 .
 This package contains the headers, CMake configuration and examples.

Package: dccl5-compiler
Section: science
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: dccl4-compiler
Description: Dynamic Compact Control Language (protoc plugin)
 The Dynamic Compact Control Language (DCCL) is a marshalling and protocol
 language for very low throughput links (e.g. acoustic, satellite, low
 frequency radio).
 .
 This package contains protoc-gen-dccl, a plugin for the Protocol Buffers
 compiler that checks the units given by (dccl.field).udunits (UDUNITS-2) or
 (dccl.field).units (Boost Units) and generates Boost Units accessors and
 mutators for them.

